+/*
+ * Give-up policy for a launcher that never exposes the target image.
+ *
+ * TryDiscoverImage() needs libapp.so in the launcher process. On builds where the desktop keeps
+ * its layout in Java and ships no such library (the four natives present are filament/gltf/jniLibs),
+ * discovery can never succeed: the retry is not slow, it is hopeless. Leaving the loop at the 50 ms
+ * start-up period spins a permanent thread - field measurement on such a device showed 28.7% of one
+ * core, i.e. a twice-a-second re-read of a 10k-line /proc/self/maps plus a symbol rescan that always
+ * returns the same "not found".
+ *
+ * The loop therefore backs off while discovery keeps failing and stops for good once the grace
+ * window is spent. A process that later loads the image still gets its one-shot chance through
+ * FastPatchOnLibraryLoad(), which runs off the linker hook rather than off this thread, so the
+ * feature is not lost on a launcher that does ship libapp.so - it is only this monitor that quits.
+ */
+constexpr uint64_t kGiveUpGraceMs = 60000;
+constexpr uint64_t kGiveUpPeriodMs = 500;
+
+/* Set once the monitor thread has stopped itself; keeps a later StartHomeTweaks from relaunching
+   a thread that is known to have nothing to do in this process. */
+std::atomic<bool> g_monitorGaveUp{false};
